+# Public browser demonstration model
+
+This static demonstration uses no private application runtime, access tokens,
+database or real business sales. `model.json` contains public synthetic model
+coefficients and the attributed, bounded 2026 Kuala Lumpur calendar.
+
+Build from the workspace root:
+
+```text
+python sites/cafe-replenishment-public/public_demo_training.py
+node sites/cafe-replenishment-public/verify_engine.mjs
+```
+
+Training reuses the local application's Python regression and temporal evaluation
+implementation. A transparent, seeded generator creates 180 daily observations
+for each of three drinks. The 28-day validation window selects a baseline or
+ridge penalty; the last 56 days are used only for rolling one-step evaluation.
+Stockout observations are excluded from normal demand fitting and lag values.
+The generated labels are independent of the fitted model's predictions.
+
+The browser regenerates a deterministic **synthetic** 180-day input history
+relative to the visitor's chosen target. The previously fitted coefficients are
+then evaluated in JavaScript. This is a public workflow demonstration, not online
+retraining or reconstruction of a real shop's history. Backtest scores describe
+the fixed synthetic training scenario and do not validate forecasts for a real
+shop. Predicted quantities are drink portions, not unique customer counts.
+
+Weather/calendar comparisons keep the model and synthetic history fixed. The
+reference uses training-average weather and an ordinary day. Two-factor Shapley
+allocation splits the weather/holiday interaction; it is a model comparison,
+not a causal business estimate.
+
+The default holiday calendar covers 2026-01-01 through 2026-12-31. Outside that
+range, or on a conditional/unknown date, automatic holiday context is rejected.
+A visitor can explicitly choose an ordinary-day or holiday **simulation**.
+The engine never silently maps an unknown holiday state to false.
+
+Stock inputs use base units (g/ml/pcs). Recipe consumption plus safety stock less
+closing usable stock and confirmed opening-time inbound gives the shortage.
+The recommendation rounds up to whole procurement packs. Owner edits are checked
+against minimum order, maximum order and storage capacity. Reductions retain a
+visible shortage; an all-zero order is not exported. Approval does not add stock.
+Supplier contacts are reserved `example.com` demo addresses. Local draft generation does not send email or call external providers. Optional visitor-owned Gmail draft saves and Runpod advisory reviews are separate explicit actions; see README_GMAIL_PUBLIC.md and README_RUNPOD_PUBLIC.md.
+
+`engine-verification.json` records six Python/JavaScript parity scenarios,
+including weather, holiday and pack boundaries. Source reference values use the
+Python materials planner's Decimal arithmetic. The check also verifies retained
+shortages, invalid edits, stale weather, unknown-year behavior and demo contacts.
