+# Optional visitor-owned Runpod review
+
+Each visitor supplies their own Serverless endpoint ID, Runpod API key and served model name. No owner's key is read or shared. Credentials stay in tab memory, pass through the same-site Netlify function for the approved request and are not written to storage, URLs or application logs.
+
+Only a narrow synthetic snapshot is sent: target date, SKU IDs, forecast units, temperature, rainfall and holiday flag. No local signature, Gmail data, supplier contact or procurement email body enters the payload. Preview shows the exact destination and payload with the key masked. A separate button explicitly approves one paid inference; there are no automatic paid submissions or retries. Returned explanations and suggested drink units are advisory only and cannot change purchasing quantities or approve an order.
+
+Limits: body 16 KiB, response 32 KiB, 1–24 SKUs, 16–1024 output tokens (512 default), temperature 0–1 and top-p 0.01–1. The proxy has a bounded request timeout. Runpod policy permits ten seconds of active inference and a five-minute total job lifetime for queue/cold start. These are safeguards, not a price or completion guarantee.
+
+Netlify rate rules plus strongly consistent Blobs cap accepted operations. A canonical endpoint/payload claim must be conditionally created and verified by exact ETag and nonce before any paid POST. Blobs retains only hashes, timestamps, nonces, counters, state and bounded job IDs, never keys, raw snapshots or review text. Missing or ambiguous storage stops paid calls.
+
+IN_QUEUE and IN_PROGRESS remain pending. Check same job manually retrieves fixed GET /v2/{endpoint}/status/{job}, using only the job ID already stored for that claim. It never resubmits inference. No automatic polling occurs. Uncertain results keep the original paid submission locked, even after reload or key rotation. Inspect Runpod directly when no job ID is available. Do not add automatic claim expiry or reset controls without reviewing duplicate billing.
+
+The backend is netlify/functions/runpod.mjs; browser hooks are initializeRunpod({getSnapshot}) and createRunpodButton() in dist/demo/runpod-ui.js. getSnapshot returns null for stale proposals, otherwise normalized synthetic data plus a local-only signature. Dispatch cafe:proposalchange when state changes and cafe:languagechange when changing language.
+
+Offline tests: node --test tests/runpod-public.test.mjs. They use fake fetch and an in-memory CAS/ETag store, never real compute. Real visitors inspect their own endpoint, key and exact request before approving any paid submission.
+
+References: https://docs.runpod.io/serverless/endpoints/send-requests ; https://github.com/runpod-workers/worker-vllm/blob/main/src/handler.py ; https://docs.netlify.com/build/data-and-storage/netlify-blobs/
+
+Paid jobs are submitted using fixed POST /v2/{endpoint}/run, which returns a job ID without waiting through cold start. Manual status checks retrieve the same job. The original claim namespace and canonical payload hash are preserved across the former sync implementation, so previously uncertain submissions stay locked.
